-- **Legacy fallback fails open on the 401 path.** `JwtManagerImpl.deleteLoginToken` (`:150`) removes `SESSION_REFRESH_COUNTDOWN`, and `securityUtil.logout(res)` runs immediately before `writeUnauthorized`. So on a 401 the `rint` cookie is gone by the time the axios response interceptor calls `refreshExpiryState()`, which then takes the missing-cookie branch and computes `LEGACY_SESSION_TTL - (now - lastActivityTime)` ≈ 15 minutes — for a session that is provably dead. The request interceptor's `recordActivity()` on the same request guarantees `lastActivityTime` is fresh, so the fallback re-arms a full window on exactly the responses that prove expiry. Not live today because the `errorKey` gate at `boot/axios.js:146` fires on that same response and tears the session down (verified), so this is defense-in-depth only — but it removes the elapsed-time safety net that previously covered a stripped/blocked response body. Fix would need a "have we ever seen `rint`?" flag to distinguish "never issued" from "just cleared". [`src/frontend/src/plugins/sessionManager.js:computeTimeUntilExpiry`, `JwtManagerImpl.java:150`]
